{
  "_about": "The Hangar (scripts/ui/hangar_stage.gd): the room the Juggernaut is shown in, on the Hangar screen and behind the main menu. \"entries\" are light presets, one each: pick one in the Hangar (Q / E or the buttons) or in Settings > Gameplay > Menus and theme. A preset has \"background\" (the colour behind the room, only seen through the door gap), \"ambient\" {color, energy}, \"exposure\", optional \"fog\" {color, density}, optional \"grade\" (shadow_shift / highlight_shift, see weather.json) and \"lights\": each {kind: spot | omni | sun, at: [x, y, z] metres with the mech standing at the origin and facing -z, look: [x, y, z] (spot and sun), color, energy, range (spot and omni), angle (spot, degrees), shadow: true | false, lamp: true draws a glowing fixture at that position}. Keep shadows to one or two lights per preset: the Iris Xe pays for each. \"stage\" holds the room and the cameras (metres, degrees); \"slots\" name the loadout slots on the Hangar screen; \"groups\" sort parts by kind in the parts list; \"menu\" is the slow sway behind the main menu (the Juggernaut stands to the right of the buttons; shift_x is how far, as a share of the picture width). Alpha 0.1.1: optional \"volumetric\" {density, albedo, anisotropy, length_m} hangs a haze in the air so spot cones show as beams (only with Settings > Graphics > Volumetric fog on); stage.room.floor_roughness sets the floor sheen (screen-space reflections follow the graphics preset).",
